# Type on the dark band (HARD — Founder Oct 31, 2026)

Look at **this** picture before you set type. Do not reuse a template Y (top / middle / bottom).

White (or gold) overlay lives on the **darkest readable band of the photo**. That is how it gets seen.

## Do this

1. Open the actual plate.
2. Find the dark wood / water / asphalt / forest / night window — the band that can hold the line.
3. Put the whole headline there. Both lines, if it wraps.
4. Afternoon 5pm plates use **white** type on that dark band.

Helper: `marketing.type_contrast.darkest_type_y`

## Tea-table lock (the example she named)

`They still have a seat at Sacred Ground.` sits **below the tabletop**, on the dark wood apron — not on the yellow linen, not on the tea.

## Never park overlay type on

- Light cloth, pale sky, cream arrows, pale doors, light sidewalk
- The bright object itself (bowl, moon, cup, card face)
- A template “middle of the photo” that happens to be the light part

## Still true

- No black/dark panel behind type
- Soft cream wash only if the dark band still fails
- Footer stays cream + ink under the photo
- Light whole-plate → black type is the old contrast rule; when she asks for white, move the line onto the dark, do not leave white on yellow
